{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":86297,"duration_api_ms":86270,"num_turns":13,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"ab1a7df4-97d1-4941-bd1a-ebc4f7b8d549","total_cost_usd":0.37680149999999996,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":31742,"cache_read_input_tokens":200708,"output_tokens":3121,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":31742,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":7,"outputTokens":3121,"cacheReadInputTokens":200708,"cacheCreationInputTokens":31742,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.37680149999999996,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"All four amendments identify real, code-verified bugs. Amendments fr-4-4e504190 and fr-4-6f70d3c3 describe the same dimensional mismatch from complementary angles (unit mismatch and invariance violation respectively) — both valid. Amendment fr-4-92b6a31f correctly identifies a test coverage gap that allowed the mismatch to go undetected. Amendment fr-4-0a3f3f58 identifies a real stability tracker reseeding omission in the v2→v3 migration path that could cause bogus instability spikes on first load of legacy saves.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-4-4e504190","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified in source: plant_growth.rs:8-11 converts half-saturation constants to mg/L via legacy_total_param_to_mg_per_l (divides by LEGACY_KINETIC_REFERENCE_VOLUME_L=20). Lines 60-61 pass raw mg totals from total_substrate_n/p() (which sum nutrient_store_mg_n_total across layers, e.g. 40+5=45 mg in seeded_example) against those mg/L constants (e.g. ~0.4 mg/L). half_saturation(45, 0.4) ≈ 0.991, making substrate limitation effectively inert. The water column path (lines 52-58) correctly uses mg/L concentrations from tan_mg_n_per_l() etc. This is a clear dimensional mismatch bug."},{"amendment_id":"fr-4-92b6a31f","decision":"accept","rationale":"The existing test explicitly zeroes out substrate_uptake_bias and clears substrate_layers, completely bypassing the substrate limitation code path (lines 60-61, 62-63 with s_norm=0). A test with nonzero substrate bias and varying substrate nutrient levels is essential to catch the dimensional mismatch and ensure substrate depletion actually limits plant growth. This is a genuine test coverage gap."},{"amendment_id":"fr-4-0a3f3f58","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: migrate_schema_v2_to_v3 (save.rs:76-82) rescales water totals via rescale_totals_for_volume but never calls stability_tracker.seed_from_water(). With #[serde(default)] on stability_tracker (state.rs:47-48), v2 saves get default baselines (temp=25, pH=7, gh=7, do=8). enforce_invariants only clamps instability_index (invariants.rs:132-133), not baselines. Both TankState::new() (state.rs:98-101) and seeded_example() (state.rs:138-139) properly call seed_from_water after construction/rescaling. The migration path is the only code path that rescales water without reseeding, creating a real risk of false instability spikes on first daily update after loading a v2 save."},{"amendment_id":"fr-4-6f70d3c3","decision":"accept","rationale":"This describes the same core bug as fr-4-4e504190 but adds the critical observation about volume/footprint invariance: because substrate limitation uses absolute mg totals (not density or concentration), a tank with twice the substrate mass appears twice as nutrient-rich regardless of tank geometry. The water column path achieves volume invariance through concentration-based units (mg/L), but the substrate path breaks this property. Both the dimensional mismatch and the invariance concern are real issues that should be addressed together."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"a5926e58-00b4-4d4e-9734-ed3fc1380963"}
